title: Quasar
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Trethewey
    given-names: Chris
    website: "https://christrethewey.dev/"
    # Add your ORCID here if you have one, e.g. orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Trethewey/quasar-sv"
url: "https://github.com/Trethewey/quasar-sv"
abstract: >-
  Quasar is a structural-variant and fusion caller for next-generation
  sequencing data, specialised for lymphoma diagnostics. It identifies
  clinically relevant translocations from aligned reads in BAM or CRAM and
  emits VCF 4.3 alongside a per-sample report. Alpha / beta: validated on a
  14-sample lymphoma cell-line cohort; not yet validated on patient samples.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - structural variants
  - gene fusions
  - lymphoma
  - cancer genomics
